pve-console-log (0.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * VMs: log the serial console via QEMU chardev logfile= (enable/disable per
    VM with pve-console-log; stored in the VM's args, root@pam only).
  * CTs: log /dev/console via lxc.console.logfile and switch cmode to console.
  * Replay the last 1000 lines when a console is opened (qm terminal and the
    dtach session PVE uses for CT consoles), rendered through python3-pyte
    when available, allowlist-filtered to text and SGR colours otherwise.
  * Tested on PVE 8.4 (QEMU 9.2, lxc 6.0); PVE 9 checked against source only.

